// The automata controller manager's part of the autotest
// (src/core/autotest_hooks.h; the manager in src/core/automata_ctlmgr.cpp).
//
// OPENSC4_TEST_AUTOMATA=1: a fingerprint part on every day,
//   ` | auto n<occupants>/<controllers> c<checksum> g<side>,<filled>,<entries>,<checksum>`:
//   the controller table (+0x58): the occupants and the controllers, each
//   occupant by its type, (not for automata) its cells and (not for props
//   and automata) its position in x and z, each controller by its kind (attractor, generator,
//   other) and its template (class ID, name, flags, radius), mixed per
//   occupant and summed (the table's order follows addresses); the grid
//   (+0x1C): its side, the cells with a controller, the entries and a sum
//   of (cell index, template). The controller time (+0x34..+0x43) follows
//   frames (A vs A differs from day 4 on): the log only. Nothing
//   of a controller's own state is read (the attractor and generator code
//   is frame-driven). The automaton table (+0x6C) is written by that code
//   on frames: it goes to the log only (`autotest: automata: ...`).
// OPENSC4_TEST_AUTOMATA=2: also, on the run day OPENSC4_TEST_AUTOMATA_DAY
//   (default 3), Write (the game's address: ours when
//   simulators.automata.ctlsave is on) into a stream of the test's own; the
//   fingerprint then carries ` w<answer>,<bytes>,<checksum>` from that day
//   on: the version (the controller time's 12 bytes left out: frames), the occupant count and
//   the sorted per-occupant controller counts (references write nothing to
//   this stream: SC4Stream::WriteReference asks the stream for the save
//   file's segment interface first). The automaton table's records go to
//   the log. Read-only: nothing of the manager or the controllers changes.
//   On the same day it also calls part a2's queries at their game addresses
//   (ours when simulators.automata.ctlquery is on): for up to 16 (occupant,
//   controller) pairs of the controller table, occupants neither automata
//   nor props (their positions follow frames), sorted by occupant and
//   controller hash (address-free): GetController by template (slot 18) and
//   by the controller's name (slot 19), slot 18 with no template, and
//   GetController near the occupant's position by name (slot 17, radius
//   64); the answers by kind and template go into the fingerprint as
//   ` q<pairs>,<checksum>` from that day on. At the same positions
//   GetRelevantControllersByWorldPos for attractors and generators (each
//   list released through ReleaseControllerList, its head freed after), the
//   composite attraction effect and, for network occupants, the commotion:
//   they read the controllers' flags, the controller time and the attractor
//   state, which follow frames: the log only (`autotest: automata: query
//   ...`). Nothing adds, removes or moves a controller or sends a message
//   (the relevant lists' references are given back).
// OPENSC4_TEST_AUTOMATA=3 (part a3c): also, on the same day, for up to 8
//   attractors and 8 generators of the controller table (occupants neither
//   automata nor props, sorted as the query pairs), at the game's addresses
//   (ours when the controller groups are on): the +4 serializable part's
//   QueryInterface 0x00517F30 (three interfaces; the AddRef it makes is
//   taken back from +0x20) and GetGZCLSID 0x00517F00; Write (the part's slot
//   3) into a stream of the test's own; a round trip: a new controller of
//   the same class from its factory reads those bytes (slot 4) and writes
//   them again, which must give the same bytes with an empty name (Read puts
//   the name into the controller's own name, Write saves the template's),
//   and its own name must be the template's; on that new controller SetLimit
//   (slot 19), SetTemplate (15) and ResetAccumulators (26), and for a
//   generator a Read of a stream with version 0 (answers 0); then it is
//   released. And the position from the occupant's lot (slot 22) of the
//   picked controller. The bytes' fixed part (versions, name, position,
//   +0x3C, the attractor's curve, the generator's +0x90) goes into the
//   fingerprint as ` s<controllers>,<checksum>,<state>`, the state checksum
//   (+0x50, +0x54, the flags, the generator's clock pairs and +0x94, the
//   automaton count: tick- and frame-driven) after it; the field values go
//   to the log (`autotest: automata: save ...`). Then the spawn (slot 41,
//   curve 1.0) of up to 4 of those generators, called directly (the tick
//   only calls it with flag 4, the camera view, which the harness never
//   sets): the automata it makes (count, +0x88, +0x90, +0x94, +0x98, each
//   new automaton's type and position) as ` p<generators>,<made>,<checksum>`;
//   with the first new automaton the generator's events 29 (kinds 4 and 0)
//   and 30 (kind 4, which takes back what 29 added), and the first
//   attractor's (one whose template keeps automata, if any) events 29 and
//   30 with kind 0 (in and out of its own list,
//   then 30 again when it is not there), the answers and list counts mixed.
//   The spawn adds automata to the city: from that day on the run is not
//   the one without the test (on both sides alike).
// OPENSC4_TEST_AUTOMATA_VEHMGR=1 (part v1, with OPENSC4_TEST_AUTOMATA=2 or
//   more): on the same day the vehicle and pedestrian managers (city slots
//   43 and 44) are queried at the game's addresses (ours when
//   simulators.automata.vehmgr is on), each manager into the fingerprint as
//   ` v<identity>,<kinds>,<scale>,<cells>,<records>,<hits>,<groups>` (the
//   vehicle manager) and ` <...>` (the pedestrian manager) from that day
//   on: QueryInterface for four interfaces on the object and through the
//   serializable part (each AddRef given back) and GetGZCLSID; for kinds 0
//   to 12 slots 73, 74, 85 (the curve's address), 86, 87 and 88 (a 16-word
//   block of the test's own, scales 1.25 and -0.75); slot 82 for the four
//   directions and the record list's hit test (0x00551630) at 12 x 12 cells
//   spread over the city (sizes from the city); the group tests 0x0054D1A0,
//   0x0054D210 and 0x0054D230 over groups 0x4000..0x4240. Slot 75 (it reads
//   the 24-hour clock), the automata of the manager's list with slots 68
//   and 41 and 0x0054D150 (which automata there are follows frames), and
//   those two tests with null go to the log only (`autotest: automata:
//   vehicle manager: ...`). Read-only.
// OPENSC4_TEST_AUTOMATA_VEHMGR=2 (part v2): also, on the same day, for each
//   manager at the game's addresses (ours when the simulators.automata.vehmgr
//   groups are on): Write (the serializable part's slot 3) into a stream of
//   the test's own; into the fingerprint as ` x<fixed>,<flags>` (the vehicle
//   manager) and ` <fixed>,<flags>` (the pedestrian manager) from that day
//   on, where fixed is the versions, the most automata, the two bools,
//   +0xA8C, the kind and the record list (the automata count and the common
//   base's table, frame-driven, go to the log only). Then a round trip: a new
//   manager of the class from its factory (0x005145A0, 0x005145D0), held by
//   one reference, reads those bytes (slot 4; the automata count zeroed in
//   the copy, the references read back as nothing) and writes them again,
//   which must give the copy with its own +0xA8C (Read drops the saved one);
//   reads of version 0, of version 2 (no record list) and of a record list
//   of version 9; AddAutomaton with none while full (its count set to the
//   most for the call, so nothing is made) and RemoveAutomaton with none
//   (flags 0 and 1); a message of a type no one handles and, for the vehicle
//   manager, 0xC9DA96E8 (its list is empty) to its message target, and the
//   vehicle manager's +4 slot 3 with a zeroed message; then the release
//   (Shutdown, not initialized, and the deleting destructor). Then the
//   pedestrian manager's gathering 0x00544F30 on the city's manager around
//   its first pedestrian with distance 0 (none is sent; the sound message
//   0xA9E3B6E3 goes out), the pedestrian's send 0x005448D0 on that
//   pedestrian to its own position (its mode changes: frame-driven state,
//   alike on both sides), and the vehicle manager's overlay stop 0x00562D60
//   on a zeroed object (nothing). The answers' AL and whether the bytes came
//   back the same are the flags. Nothing else of the city's managers
//   changes.
// OPENSC4_TEST_AUTOMATA_VEHMGR=3 (part v3): also, on the same day, for each
//   manager at the game's addresses (ours when the simulators.automata.vehmgr
//   groups are on), into the fingerprint as ` y<fixed>,<flags>` (the vehicle
//   manager) and ` <fixed>,<flags>` (the pedestrian manager) from that day
//   on: on a new manager of the class from its factory, three records by
//   slot 70 (and none without an object) with two building occupants of the
//   controller table (the least by OccupantHash), slot 55 taking the first
//   occupant's records out (0x0054DB50 moves the rest down) and then the
//   second's, the records hashed after each step with the occupants as
//   indices; slot 69 and slot 52 (with the first of two network occupants,
//   the cells' occupants at 12 x 12 places spread over the cells object's
//   rectangle) on its empty automata list (their AL and
//   whether EAX's upper bytes are the list head's); slot 72 for kinds 0, 7,
//   8 and 11 (zero, or slot 88 with a 16-word block of the test's own); then
//   the release. The record copy 0x0054DB50 on records of the test's own.
//   For the vehicle manager, the tuning map's insert and lookup (0x00555350,
//   0x00555400) on a map of the test's own (two records; no key that is not
//   there, which would add a record of stack leftovers in the game), then
//   the lookup of each key of the game's map 0x00B21D60 (read-only), its
//   keys and records hashed. The log only (`autotest: automata: ... manager
//   frames`), on the city's manager, since which automata there are, the
//   cells' contents and the manager's generator follow frames:
//   GetRandomCreationPoint (slot 16) at four places spread over the city
//   (sizes from the city) with the generator (+0x50) seeded for the calls
//   and put back after; the occupant's position (0x0054DD50) and slot 72 for
//   the kinds of +0xA88's tables at the two network occupants; then AddAutomaton
//   with none while there is room (the branch that makes one from the
//   class's pool) and the one made, the list's last, removed again (slot 8
//   with 1). Then the frame work the harness's saves leave off (+0x4C, the
//   manager's own generation, is clear in them and they have no records):
//   the kind sweep (slot 76) through each kind of the list, with the
//   generator seeded for it and put back after (the harness's stopwatch
//   counts its reads, so a call walks a few cells: it is called again until
//   the kind's walk is through, at most 40000 calls), and records as slot 53
//   makes them (the IDs of property 0xE9AEE3DA / 0xE9AEE3DC of the first
//   building occupant of the controller table that has it, by
//   OccupantHash; for the vehicle manager also the drawn record 0x4206)
//   spent by slot 84 with a time of 1, then what is left of them released
//   and cleared. These add automata to the city and take some away: from
//   that day on the run is not the one without the test (on both sides
//   alike).
// OPENSC4_TEST_AUTOMATA_VEHICLE=1 (part vb1, with OPENSC4_TEST_AUTOMATA=2 or
//   more): on the same day the automaton base and cSC4Vehicle are driven at
//   the game's addresses (ours when simulators.automata.vehicle is on) on
//   objects of the test's own, into the fingerprint as
//   ` V<object>,<accessors>,<queries>,<nearest>,<flags>`. The automata's
//   generator (0x00B21D78, 0x9C8 bytes) is saved and seeded first and put
//   back after, so the drawn times are the same on both sides and the game's
//   draws do not change. Four vehicles from the factory (0x005148E0), each
//   held by one reference: their fields after construction (vtables, type,
//   the draw, the smoothed value, the base's and the vehicle's fields, the
//   deques empty); a base object (SC4::operator_new, 0x005544D0, then
//   0x005552F0); QueryInterface for six interfaces at both addresses and
//   through the +4 part (each AddRef given back) and GetGZCLSID; the
//   accessors (addresses as offsets, the manager compared with city slot 43,
//   the deque's back with the expected address); slot 146 at points around
//   16 x the byte 0x00B21CB8, slot 155 at points near and far, 0x0054EA30
//   over its byte, state, flag and an occupant of the test's (slot 0x58),
//   slot 171 for nine directions with and without a network of the test's
//   (slot 0xD4, three side masks), slot 152 with a network part of the
//   test's answering yes and no (the no then asks 0x00B43D54's slot 0x3C
//   with no occupant, which answers null); 0x0050AAF0 on a manager of the
//   test's whose list holds the four vehicles at set positions, radii and
//   flags for three margins; 0x0054FC30 with keys 0 and 1 (no list). The
//   fakes' arguments are mixed (the bytes the game passes with stack above
//   them as bytes). Then each vehicle's references are cleared and its last
//   reference released (the deleting destructor 0x00562A90 through +0xC's
//   slot 22: the deques, the pool). To the log only: for up to 24 of the
//   city's vehicles (manager +0x44; which there are follows frames) slots
//   146, 150, 138, 0x0054EA30 and slot 123 with margins 0 and 2, and the
//   first one's network part's vtable and slot 0x90. Part vb2 adds
//   `,<setters>,<save>,<texts>,<life>` to the token, on the same four
//   vehicles before their release: the setters (slots 154, 178, 180, 158
//   of both classes, 184, 159, 160, 149, 124; 0x0055CA60 with null, a pool
//   block and another size); 25 elements pushed on the +0x204 deque
//   (0x00554230, 0x00553780) and released (0x00554640), 12 more emptied
//   (0x00554280); three records on a record list of the test's
//   (0x00554160); Write (0x0055F640) into a ByteOStream with three +0x27C
//   elements (the core's part to the log only), the stream given 50 route
//   cells and read into the second vehicle (0x0055BCF0; and twice with a
//   wrong version), the second written again; both debug texts on two
//   vehicles with and without a model key; Init and Shutdown of both
//   classes on the third and fourth (their deques and +0x258/+0x25C given
//   objects of the test's that count their references), then slots 172 and
//   135. Objects of the test's count their references into the hashes.
//   Part vb3 adds `,<move>,<frame>,<enter>`: a base object (0x005544D0)
//   whose vtable is a copy of the base's with slot 174 answering a vehicle
//   manager of the test's, its byte +0x33's low bits cleared (else the
//   core's slot 16 would index it in the occupant manager) and the automata
//   flag 0x100000 on (else slot 16 would put it on the view's update list),
//   driven with the city global 0x00B43CEC pointing at a city of the test's
//   (a traffic network map of the test's, a size of 2048 x 1024, cells of
//   16; other slots counted into the flags as 0x200). move: SetDestination for six targets, slot
//   157 on two paths for five offsets, slot 133 along a five-point path for
//   seven steps and five start indices (offsets 0 and 1.25), slot 151 at
//   three places with the flags 0x10 and 8 and an automaton ahead of the
//   test's, 50 route cells pushed and 49 popped (0x00551F70), slot 170 over
//   three side masks and four directions, 0x0054E6F0 for four sides.
//   enter: slot 132 into a lane, a tunnel (QueryInterface 0x8A4BD52B), no
//   network part, a part without a path and none; slot 131 to four
//   occupants, with a path and without, exact or not; slot 134 at the
//   default point and over five occupants and three +0xA4 cases; slot 142
//   over six route cells with a cell list of three occupants. frame: slot
//   129 for 12 frames of 0.25 s, flat or not, with an automaton ahead or
//   not, its early way out, steps of 0 and -2 (stopped, removed); slot 130
//   towards five goals with the automata flag 0x20000 on and off and the
//   map's slot 44 answering yes and no, four frames of 0.5 s each. The
//   fakes' calls and reference counts go into the hashes; the base object
//   is deleted with its references cleared and +0x98 and +0x33 put back.
//   Part vb4 adds `,<states>,<ahead>,<steps>` (the flags 8 when it ran): a
//   second base object held the same way, its vtable the base's with the
//   core's slots the vb4 code calls on frames (13, 19, 52, 53, 61, 62, 67,
//   73, 79, 83, 86 to 89, 102, 103, 105, 131, 132, 134, 141, 142, 159, 160)
//   and the vb4 and vb3 slots driven at their own addresses (109, 129, 130,
//   148, 163 to 166) answering a probe of the test's that mixes each call;
//   the city global and 0x00B43D54 point at the test's while the calls run,
//   0x00B09964 is set for slot 163. states: 0x0054E380; slot 72 over four
//   smoothed values and the probe's answers (96 calls); slot 109 with no
//   state and four current ones; slot 163 over five timers, the flags 0x20
//   and 0x80 and the map's wait answer; slot 164 with and without a speed
//   over three timers; slots 110 and 111 for null, 0x1E, 5, 0xD, 0x15 and 7,
//   and 0x10 without an occupant, on a lane and on a tunnel lane answering
//   its slot 9 (the game's entries object 0x00B22C30 adds and removes the
//   entry; its handles are not mixed); 0x00552B80 and 0x0054ECC0 on a record
//   list of the test's; slot 145 with an empty route and a 45-cell one.
//   ahead: slot 147 on an occupant's eight automata of the test's and its
//   neighbours (depths 1, 0, -1), with the flag 0x2000 and without an
//   occupant; slot 148 over three and one steps and the neighbour; slot 161
//   over three automata ahead, seven flag sets and five ways (the byte +0x33,
//   slot 141, the part's slot 13, the state 0xD); slot 162 over chains of 1
//   to 55 and three occupant types; slot 173 over five occupants and two
//   keys. steps: 0x00504C40 and 0x00553720 over 25 steps; slot 169 over
//   nine key counts with and without the flag 0x40, from the first and the
//   last step; slot 167 over three neighbours, two side masks, three tries
//   and three ways; slot 168 over an empty route, one cell, a cell ahead in
//   each direction and 46 pops of 50 cells; slot 166 with slots 167 and 168
//   the test's (fails, last steps, no occupant), then the game's once; slot
//   165 over nine cases (no manager, no occupant, the flag 0x2000, a last
//   step, two to four steps, slot 88). To the log only: the tuning floats
//   0x00B21C84, 0x00B21C74 and 0x00B21D2C, slot 175's byte.
//   Part ro1 (the other road vehicles, src/core/automata_roadveh.cpp) adds
//   `,<robject>,<rsave>,<rlife>,<rflags>` after vb8's and ad1 to ad3's: one
//   object of each of the six classes from its factory (the trailer, the
//   bus, the getaway van, the carjacked vehicle, the tank, the limo; rflags
//   1, 0x10 when a factory failed): their fields, GetGZCLSID, QueryInterface
//   through slot 0 for four IDs (the trailer's also at its address); the
//   trailer's slot 66 without and with cars of the test's, slots 193 and 194.
//   rsave (rflags 2): each class written by its Write and by cSC4Vehicle's
//   (the bytes after cSC4Vehicle's part, the version word, whether the rest
//   is cSC4Vehicle's), read into a new object with its version and one more
//   (the tank's 2, 1, 0, 3 and one byte short; the trailer also cut after
//   its first word), the bus's, the carjacked vehicle's and the tank's Read
//   on an empty stream; the tank written with models of the test's in its
//   model vector (indices found, then none). rlife (rflags 8): the
//   trailer's Init and Shutdown (its cars and occupant of the test's); the
//   limo's Init five times with its +0xC vtable a copy whose GetProperty
//   answers a property of the test's for 0xEC15654A (absent, 1 to 4 floats;
//   rflags 4); the tank's Init twice, its debug text with a shot of the
//   test's, Shutdown, and three more tanks with the byte +0x3C and indices
//   that do not hold. Then each object released (the deleting destructors).
//   To the log only: whether the tank's Init made a shot effect.
//   Part ro2 (the frames, src/core/automata_roadveh.cpp) adds `,<rframe>`
//   after rflags (30 fields): one object of each class from its factory, its
//   main vtable a copy whose slots the test answers (vb's probe; cars,
//   managers, services and the network service of the test's swapped into
//   the globals for the calls, nothing of the real city read or changed but
//   the traffic map pointer and the core's generator, seeded as for vb).
//   The trailer's slot 198 on nine segments; slot 192 with a null end and a
//   growing vector; slot 73 with null, itself, its car and another's car
//   under six flag sets; slot 95 with no template and lists of 0 to 3 words;
//   slot 132 with no occupant; slot 195 over seven cases and a second car;
//   slot 197 over six runs of three cars and one car on the trailer's rear
//   point; slot 196 over nine runs of the path and a deque of three
//   elements in two blocks (used up, blocked, empty, no path, no cars); slot
//   72 over five runs. The bus's slot 164 over ten runs (the riders'
//   answers and the generator's draws) and 172 over six; the carjacked
//   vehicle's slot 101 twice; the van's 101 over thirteen cases; the limo's
//   121 over eight; the tank's 127. The calls' hash and a bit for each of the
//   15 reached are mixed in; rflags 0x20 when all 15 ran, 0x40 when a
//   factory failed. Log line: "ro2 rframe".
//   Part ro3a (the tank on frames) adds `,<rtank>` after rframe (31
//   fields): a tank from its factory, its main vtable ro2's copy with slots
//   18, 19, 56, 67, 100 and 102 the test's (the controls, the template and
//   its entry of the test's; for the state 0x10 slot 67 makes the state 7
//   for cSC4Vehicle's and the base's slot 110 and slot 102 makes it 0x10
//   again, so the base's records and the city's entries are not touched).
//   Slot 110 over five states; slot 115 over thirteen frames (cSC4Vehicle's
//   early answers, the mouse point, the occupant, the template, the turn
//   keys on six headings); slot 121 over twenty-three (slot 18, the
//   turret's range, the velocity key, the pointer picked by a 0x00B43DC4 of
//   the test's, the fire key with a barrel model, shot and attachments
//   vtable of the test's, the barrel and velocity keys, the sound timers,
//   which are put back after). The U-Drive sounds are the game's; 0x13, 0xC
//   and 0xF are stopped after. rflags 0x80 when all 3 ran, 0x100 when the
//   factory or the sound service failed. Log line: "ro3a rtank".
//   Part ro3b (the tank's frame) adds `,<rturret>` after rtank (32
//   fields): the tank's slot 72 over thirteen frames on a tank of the
//   factory's (ro2's vtable copy, slots 194 and 197 the test's): the byte
//   +0x340 clear, each model missing, then both models of the test's on
//   eight headings (one not of unit length, one straight up) and angles;
//   twice the turret model's call changes the axis, the angles and the
//   heading before the barrel model's turns; then 256 frames on drawn
//   headings and angles (a fixed LCG). Each answer is mixed whole
//   (slot 197's EAX with AL 1). rflags 0x200 when all 13 ran, 0x400 when
//   the factory failed. Log line: "ro3b rturret".
//   Part tr1 (the trains, src/core/automata_trains.cpp) adds
//   `,<tobject>,<tsave>,<tlife>,<tflags>` after rturret (36 fields): one
//   train car, train and mass transit train from their factories (tflags 1,
//   0x10 when a factory failed): their fields, GetGZCLSID, QueryInterface
//   through slot 0 for six IDs and both QueryInterfaces at their addresses,
//   the car pool with another size and a null block; the train's slots 175
//   and 193 to 196 over nine steps on cars of the test's (a null one among
//   them; tflags 8); the car's slot 50 without and with a train of the
//   test's, slot 65 by three states (a car that is its own train has a
//   recorder in its slot 65), slot 120 with a disaster service of the
//   test's over six values of the controls' +0x10 (the automata flag 1 set,
//   so the core's slot 120 answers at once). tsave (tflags 2): each class
//   written by its Write and cSC4Vehicle's, read back as written, with each
//   version word 3, cut by the last word (the trains) and empty. tlife
//   (tflags 4): the car's Init (groups through a copy of its +4 vtable)
//   twice and on two more cars; eight trains (the last a mass transit train
//   through its slots 3 and 4) initialised over the group sets and shut
//   down (occupants of the test's in both deques, an occupant and cars,
//   the network service of the test's or none). The test's objects' calls
//   are mixed into tobject and tlife. Log line: "tr1 tobject".
//   Part tr2a (the trains' frames) adds `,<tframe>` before tflags (37
//   fields): a car, a train and a mass transit train of the factories with
//   vtable copies (ro2's probe slots and vb4's, the state, controls, slots
//   65, 166, 169 and 192 the test's), vb4's vehicle manager, the city and
//   0x00B43D54 the test's (slots 38 and 39 added), the lot manager
//   0x00B43D08 the test's: the car's slot 110 over the states 0x14 (its
//   +0x28 object or none), 0x1E and 0xD, as a car and a train, with a train
//   of the test's or none in the state 0x14 or not and its controls; the
//   train's 110 and 111 over the states 0x10 (by the template's entry),
//   0x1E, 0xD and 0x14 on cars of the test's; slot 73 on its cars and
//   others; slot 121 by the state's +0x7C and +0x80; slot 125 on drawn
//   headings (a fixed LCG) with the slope tuning the test's; both slots 172
//   over stop chains and groups; slot 165 of both (the wanted count, the
//   deques before and after, the lots by direction); slot 65 on drawn
//   headings (the generator clock-seeded at the game's site); the car's and
//   the train's slot 132 over occupants answering 0x4A10AFC2 or not. tflags
//   0x20 when it ran, 0x40 when a factory failed, 0x80 when the city's
//   other slots were called. Log line: "tr2a tframe".
//   Part tr2b (the train's movement) adds `,<tmove>` before tflags (38
//   fields): a train of the factory with tr2a's vtable copy and slots 34,
//   125, 132, 133, 151, 171 and 182 the test's (fixed answers and points,
